# Rarity of magic items: p. 206-207 ("Rarity"), in the item header, e.g. p. 207 "Wondrous item,
# rare (requires attunement)", p. 233 "Potion, common", p. 252 "artifact"; the id of common is
# common-rarity, common is the language
Rules/Term/common-rarity: common
Rules/Term/uncommon: uncommon
Rules/Term/rare: rare
Rules/Term/very-rare: very rare
Rules/Term/legendary: legendary
Rules/Term/artifact: artifact

# Item categories: weapons p. 64-66 (simple and martial, melee and ranged, the properties p. 65),
# armor p. 62-64 (light, medium, heavy armor; shield p. 64), adventuring gear p. 66-69 (ammunition,
# arcane focus, druidic focus, holy symbol p. 69), equipment packs p. 70, tools p. 70 (artisan's
# tools, gaming set, musical instrument), mounts and vehicles p. 71-72 ("Tack, Harness, and Drawn
# Vehicles", "Waterborne Vehicles"), trade goods p. 72, food and drink p. 73 ("Food, Drink, and
# Lodging"), poisons p. 204 (contact, ingested, inhaled, injury); magic items p. 207 ("Armor, potion,
# ring, rod, scroll, staff, wand, weapon, or wondrous item"). Weapon groups: p. 64 "swords, axes,
# and polearms", p. 223 "Weapon (any sword)", p. 211 "Weapon (any axe)", p. 95 "a bow or a
# crossbow"; the groups of the weapons are our reading. Ammunition kinds p. 69 ("Arrows (20)",
# "Crossbow bolts (20)", "Sling bullets (20)", "Blowgun needles (50)"). A trait with the id of its
# parent after a slash replaces the label of the parent ("martial weapon", "medium armor").
